# explainer-press (M11): what ? opened closes as the focus leaves the row, here by a press
# elsewhere: k's box clicked, Shift+Tab back to it, ? (explainer-key), then a press on the top bar
# (760, 48) takes the focus from the box (to the page, as a press on what takes no focus does) and
# the explainer goes back into its caret. Inputs and closing shots fall on the 16 ms grid: a closing
# explainer is gone at its exit's end, React's at that instant, the port's from its next frame. ? is
# pressed with Shift held, as a US keyboard sends it: React sees the key ?, SDL hands the port /
# with Shift (SDL 3's key events carry the key unshifted); Playwright's ? alone has no Shift, and
# Shift+/ reaches the page as /.
size 1440 900
density 2
scheme dark
mode dark
theme arctic-ice
wait 2000
click 383 468
wait 16
tab shift
wait 16
hold Shift
key ?
release Shift
wait 1104
click 760 48
shot press-0000
wait 96
shot press-0096
wait 112
shot press-gone
